sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-16> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Skeletal form, as produced by growth, is to a very large extent determined by mechanical stress: material is laid down along the lines of stress so as to avoid shear, from the trabeculae within each bone to the arrangement of the bones in the whole skeleton.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Skeletal form is largely a diagram of mechanical stress";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XVI, “On Form and Mechanical Efficiency”; topic “Skeletal form as a diagram of stress”. Scope: vertebrate skeletons, from bone microstructure to whole-skeleton architecture"
}
